---
title: Dynamic Mobile QBE Filter
description: Replace server-side keywords like SYSDAY with dynamic values for mobile offline filtering
keywords: 'ibm,maximo,maf,mobile,qbe,filter,sysday,offline,datasource'
date: 13 January 2026
hiddenFromSearch: false
difficulty: complex
---

## Overview

Server-side keywords like `SYSDAY`, `SYSDATE`, and `&PERSONID&` work perfectly when querying the Maximo server through REST API. However, in mobile disconnected mode, these keywords cannot be processed because there's no server connection. This guide shows how to replace these keywords with dynamic values that work in offline mode.

**Use Cases:**
- Filtering work orders by current date in mobile offline mode
- Using dynamic user information in mobile queries
- Creating date-based filters that work offline
- Implementing time-sensitive filters for mobile apps

**Prerequisites:**
- Understanding of [datasources](/datasources-guide)
- Knowledge of [mobile QBE filters](/faq#how-to-filter-with-datasource)
- Familiarity with [lifecycle events](/concepts#event-lifecycle)

**Important Note:**
> Mobile QBE filters only work on data already downloaded to the device. They filter the local database, not the server.

## Implementation

### Step 1: Identify the server keyword to replace

Common server keywords that need replacement:
- `SYSDAY` - Current date (no time component)
- `SYSDATE` - Current date and time
- `&PERSONID&` - Current user's person ID
- `&USERID&` - Current user ID
- `&SITEID&` - Current site ID

**Example server query:**
```xml
<!-- This works on server but NOT in mobile offline mode -->
<maximo-datasource id="todayWorkDS" 
                   where="schedstart <= SYSDAY"
                   mobile-qbe-filter="{{'schedstart': '<=SYSDAY'}}"/>
```

### Step 2: Replace with dynamic value using state

**Option A: Using Application State**

**XML Configuration:**
```xml
<maximo-datasource id="todayWorkDS" 
                   object-structure="MXAPIWODETAIL"
                   where="schedstart <= SYSDAY"
                   mobile-qbe-filter="{{'schedstart': '<='+app.state.currentDate}}">
  <schema>
    <attribute name="wonum" searchable="true" id="attr_001"/>
    <attribute name="schedstart" id="attr_002"/>
    <attribute name="description" id="attr_003"/>
  </schema>
</maximo-datasource>
```

**AppCustomizations.js:**
```js
/**
 * Custom Application Logic
 */
const TAG = 'DynamicFilter';

class AppCustomizations {
    /**
     * Initialize application
     * @param {Application} app - The application instance
     */
    applicationInitialized(app) {
        this.app = app;
    }

    /**
     * Set dynamic filter values when datasource initializes
     * @param {Datasource} datasource - The datasource being initialized
     * @param {Object} owner - The owner of the datasource
     * @param {Application} app - The application instance
     */
    onDatasourceInitialized(datasource, owner, app) {
        if (datasource.name === 'todayWorkDS') {
            // Convert current date to ISO format for mobile QBE
            const today = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(new Date());

            // Store in application state for use in mobile-qbe-filter binding
            app.state.currentDate = today;

            this.app.log.d(TAG, `Set current date for mobile filter: ${today}`);
        }
    }
}

export default AppCustomizations;
```

### Step 3: Alternative - Update datasource query directly

**Option B: Direct Query Update**

**AppCustomizations.js:**
```js
const TAG = 'DynamicFilter';

class AppCustomizations {
    applicationInitialized(app) {
        this.app = app;
    }

    /**
     * Update datasource query with dynamic values
     * @param {Datasource} datasource - The datasource being initialized
     * @param {Object} owner - The owner of the datasource
     * @param {Application} app - The application instance
     */
    onDatasourceInitialized(datasource, owner, app) {
        if (datasource.name === 'todayWorkDS') {
            // Get current date in ISO format
            const today = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(new Date());

            // Update the mobile QBE filter directly
            datasource.updateBaseQuery({
                "mobileQbeFilter": {
                    "schedstart": `<=${today}`
                }
            });

            this.app.log.d(TAG, `Updated mobile QBE filter with date: ${today}`);
        }
    }
}

export default AppCustomizations;
```

## Complete Examples

### Example 1: Filter by Date Range

```js
const TAG = 'DateRangeFilter';

class AppCustomizations {
    applicationInitialized(app) {
        this.app = app;
    }

    /**
     * Set up date range filter for mobile
     * @param {Datasource} datasource - The datasource
     * @param {Object} owner - The owner
     * @param {Application} app - The application
     */
    onDatasourceInitialized(datasource, owner, app) {
        if (datasource.name === 'weekWorkDS') {
            const today = new Date();
            const weekFromNow = new Date();
            weekFromNow.setDate(today.getDate() + 7);

            // Convert to ISO format
            const startDate = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(today);
            const endDate = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(weekFromNow);

            // Update filter for work orders in next 7 days
            datasource.updateBaseQuery({
                "mobileQbeFilter": {
                    "schedstart": `>=${startDate}`,
                    "schedfinish": `<=${endDate}`
                }
            });

            this.app.log.d(TAG, `Filtering work orders from ${startDate} to ${endDate}`);
        }
    }
}

export default AppCustomizations;
```

### Example 2: Filter by Current User

```js
const TAG = 'UserFilter';

class AppCustomizations {
    applicationInitialized(app) {
        this.app = app;
    }

    /**
     * Filter by current user's labor code
     * @param {Datasource} datasource - The datasource
     * @param {Object} owner - The owner
     * @param {Application} app - The application
     */
    onDatasourceInitialized(datasource, owner, app) {
        if (datasource.name === 'myWorkDS') {
            // Get current user information
            const userInfo = app.client.userInfo;
            const laborCode = userInfo?.labor?.laborcode;

            if (laborCode) {
                // Filter work orders assigned to current user
                datasource.updateBaseQuery({
                    "mobileQbeFilter": {
                        "assignment[0].laborcode": laborCode
                    }
                });

                this.app.log.d(TAG, `Filtering work orders for labor: ${laborCode}`);
            } else {
                this.app.log.w(TAG, 'No labor code found for current user');
            }
        }
    }
}

export default AppCustomizations;
```

### Example 3: Multiple Dynamic Filters

```js
const TAG = 'MultiFilter';

class AppCustomizations {
    applicationInitialized(app) {
        this.app = app;
    }

    /**
     * Set up multiple dynamic filters
     * @param {Datasource} datasource - The datasource
     * @param {Object} owner - The owner
     * @param {Application} app - The application
     */
    onDatasourceInitialized(datasource, owner, app) {
        if (datasource.name === 'priorityWorkDS') {
            const today = new Date();
            const todayISO = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(today);
            const userInfo = app.client.userInfo;
            const siteId = userInfo?.defaultSite;

            // Build complex filter
            const mobileFilter = {
                "schedstart": `<=${todayISO}`,
                "status_maxvalue": "!=COMP,CAN,CLOSE",
                "wopriority": "<=2"
            };

            // Add site filter if available
            if (siteId) {
                mobileFilter.siteid = siteId;
            }

            datasource.updateBaseQuery({
                "mobileQbeFilter": mobileFilter
            });

            this.app.log.d(TAG, `Applied multi-filter: ${JSON.stringify(mobileFilter)}`);
        }
    }
}

export default AppCustomizations;
```

### Example 4: Refreshing Filter on Page Resume

```js
const TAG = 'RefreshFilter';

class AppCustomizations {
    applicationInitialized(app) {
        this.app = app;
    }

    /**
     * Refresh date filter when page resumes
     * @param {Page} page - The page
     * @param {Application} app - The application
     */
    pageResumed(page, app) {
        if (page.name === 'workOrderList') {
            const datasource = page.datasources['todayWorkDS'];

            if (datasource) {
                // Update to current date (in case app was open overnight)
                const today = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(new Date());

                datasource.updateBaseQuery({
                    "mobileQbeFilter": {
                        "schedstart": `<=${today}`
                    }
                });

                // Reload data with new filter
                datasource.load();

                this.app.log.d(TAG, `Refreshed filter with current date: ${today}`);
            }
        }
    }
}

export default AppCustomizations;
```

## Validation & Testing

**How to verify:**

1. **Test in connected mode:**
   - Verify server-side where clause works
   - Check data loads correctly

2. **Test in offline mode:**
   - Enable airplane mode or disconnect network
   - Navigate to the page with filtered datasource
   - Verify data filters correctly using local database

3. **Test date boundaries:**
   - Change device date/time
   - Verify filter updates appropriately
   - Test edge cases (midnight, timezone changes)

4. **Check logs:**
   ```
   ?_graphite_logLevel=debug
   ```
   Look for your TAG messages in console

**Common Issues:**

- **Issue:** Filter doesn't work in mobile offline mode
  - **Cause:** Using server keywords (SYSDAY) in mobile-qbe-filter
  - **Solution:** Replace with dynamic values as shown above

- **Issue:** Date format doesn't match
  - **Cause:** Incorrect date format for mobile QBE
  - **Solution:** Use `app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO()`

- **Issue:** Filter works on first load but not after
  - **Cause:** Filter not refreshed when data changes
  - **Solution:** Update filter in pageResumed or when needed

- **Issue:** Nested attributes don't filter
  - **Cause:** Mobile QBE only filters top-level object
  - **Solution:** Use aliases for nested properties

## Best Practices

**✅ Do:**
- Use `app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO()` for date formatting
- Store dynamic values in application state for reusability
- Log filter values for debugging
- Test both connected and offline modes
- Refresh filters when page resumes (for date-based filters)
- Handle missing user information gracefully

**❌ Don't:**
- Use server keywords (SYSDAY, &PERSONID&) in mobile-qbe-filter
- Hardcode dates or user information
- Forget to test in offline mode
- Assume nested properties work in mobile QBE
- Use complex expressions that work on server but not mobile

**Performance Considerations:**
- Mobile QBE filters are applied client-side (fast)
- Filters only affect already-downloaded data
- Complex filters may impact performance on large datasets
- Consider pre-filtering with saved queries to reduce data download

**Mobile-Specific Notes:**
- Mobile QBE filters only work on local database
- Cannot filter on nested object properties directly
- Use aliases for nested properties you need to filter
- Filters are case-sensitive

## Date Formatting Reference

```js
// Get current date/time
const now = new Date();

// Convert to ISO format for mobile QBE
const isoDate = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(now);
// Result: "2026-01-13T00:00:00+00:00"

// Get date only (no time)
const dateOnly = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(new Date(now.setHours(0,0,0,0)));

// Get date 7 days from now
const future = new Date();
future.setDate(future.getDate() + 7);
const futureISO = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(future);

// Get date 7 days ago
const past = new Date();
past.setDate(past.getDate() - 7);
const pastISO = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(past);
```

## Comparison: Server vs Mobile Filtering

| Aspect | Server (where clause) | Mobile (QBE filter) |
|--------|----------------------|---------------------|
| **Keywords** | SYSDAY, &PERSONID& work | Must use dynamic values |
| **Processing** | Server-side | Client-side (local DB) |
| **Data Scope** | All data in Maximo | Only downloaded data |
| **Performance** | Depends on server | Fast (local) |
| **Nested Properties** | Supported | Limited (use aliases) |
| **When to Use** | Connected mode | Offline mode |

## Related Resources

**Prerequisites:**
- [Datasources Guide](/datasources-guide) - Understanding datasources
- [FAQ - How to filter with datasource](/faq#how-to-filter-with-datasource)
- [Basic Concepts - Event Lifecycle](/concepts#event-lifecycle)

**Related Practices:**
- [Client-side Datasource Filtering](/simple/client-side-datasource-filtering) - In-memory filtering
- [Modify Default Queries](/simple/modify-default-queries) - Saved queries

**Next Steps:**
- [Restrict Complete Status](/complex/restrict-complete-status) - Complex validation
- [Additional Logic](/complex/additional-logic) - Extending methods

**External Documentation:**
- [JavaScript Date Object](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date)
- [ISO 8601 Date Format](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601)

## Additional Notes

**Timezone Considerations:**

Mobile devices may be in different timezones. Consider using UTC:

```js
// Get UTC date
const utcDate = new Date();
const utcISO = app.dataFormatter.convertDatetoISO(
    new Date(utcDate.getTime() + utcDate.getTimezoneOffset() * 60000)
);
```

**Debugging Mobile Filters:**

Enable detailed logging to see filter application:

```js
onDatasourceInitialized(datasource, owner, app) {
    if (datasource.name === 'myDS') {
        const filter = {/* your filter */};

        // Log before applying
        this.app.log.d(TAG, `Applying filter: ${JSON.stringify(filter)}`);

        datasource.updateBaseQuery({"mobileQbeFilter": filter});

        // Log datasource state
        this.app.log.d(TAG, `Datasource query: ${JSON.stringify(datasource.baseQuery)}`);
    }
}
```

**Testing Offline Mode:**

1. Load data while connected
2. Enable airplane mode
3. Navigate to filtered page
4. Verify filter works on local data
5. Check console for any errors

